FILE-07: write small input values with significant digits, not 4 decimals

saveinpfile() writes pipe roughness, valve settings, pattern factors,
curve points and control settings and levels with %.4f, so any value
below 0.00005 is saved as 0 and values below 0.01 lose digits: a pump
curve flow of 0.00045 m3/s comes back as 0.0004. Use %.10g for these
values. It keeps 10 significant digits, so it never keeps fewer digits
than %.4f for values below 1e6, and it drops the trailing zeros that
%.4f added. Other fields keep their formats.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply FILE-07_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/inpfile.c b/src/inpfile.c
index ad24244..9db4075 100644
--- a/src/inpfile.c
+++ b/src/inpfile.c
@@ -218,7 +218,7 @@ int saveinpfile(Project *pr, const char *fname)
